\subsubsection{Amorphous}
The tarrasque can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.
\subsubsection{Antimagic Cone}
The tarrasque's eyes create an area of antimagic, as in the \textit{antimagic field} spell, in a 150-foot-cone. At the start of each of its turns, the tarrasque decides which way the cone faces.
\subsubsection{Breath Weapon}
The tarrasque can use its action or spend 3 legendary actions to breathe energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a DC 27 saving throw, taking 91 (26d6) damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The ability used for the saving throw and the type of damage are different for each tarrasque and chosen or rolled on the Tarrasque Breath Weapon table. The  tarrasque also gains immunity to the damage type of its breath weapon if it does not already have it.
